---
import Product from '../layouts/Product.astro';
import InstallCommand from '../components/InstallCommand.astro';
import config from '../data/site.json';
import { href, guide, repository, releases, download } from '../data/links';
import { readSnapshot } from '../../../scripts/download-stats.mjs';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
const stats = readSnapshot(fileURLToPath(new URL('../../public/stats/downloads.json', import.meta.url)));
if (stats && stats.repository !== config.releaseRepository) throw new Error('Wrong statistics repository');
const totals = new Map<string, number>();
for (const asset of stats?.assets ?? []) totals.set(asset.version, (totals.get(asset.version) ?? 0) + asset.downloads);
const total = [...totals.values()].reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0);
const samples = [
  { name: 'LaTeX', id: 'paper', detail: 'A simple trajectory' },
  { name: 'Typst', id: 'typst', detail: 'Motion and least squares' },
  { name: 'TikZ', id: 'tikz', detail: 'A triangle and a workflow' },
  { name: 'CeTZ', id: 'cetz', detail: 'Vector sketches in Typst' },
];
const app = `brew install --cask ${config.homebrewCask}`;
const converters = 'brew install typst pdf2svg poppler ghostscript';
const full = `${app} mactex-no-gui\n${converters}`;
const minimal = `${app} basictex\n${converters}\nsudo /Library/TeX/texbin/tlmgr update --self\nsudo /Library/TeX/texbin/tlmgr install latexmk preview pdfcrop pgf mathtools`;
---
<Product title="Download" description="FerMatter for macOS: release status, requirements, example projects, and download statistics.">
  <header class="page-intro"><h1>Download</h1><p class="lead">Apple Silicon Mac · macOS 14 or later</p></header>
  <div class="download-layout">
    <section class="download-section" id="mac">
      <h2>{config.releaseAvailable ? `FerMatter ${config.releaseName}` : 'Development preview'}</h2>
      <p>{config.releaseAvailable ? 'Download the disk image and drag FerMatter into Applications.' : 'A signed, notarized public installer is not available yet.'}</p>
      {config.releaseAvailable && !config.releaseNotarized && <p><strong>Not notarized.</strong> If macOS blocks first launch, try opening the app once, then use <strong>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Open Anyway</strong>. <a href="https://support.apple.com/102445">Apple’s instructions ↗</a></p>}
      <div class="actions">
        {config.releaseAvailable && <><a class="button primary" href={download}>Download DMG ↓</a><a href={`${download}.sha256`}>SHA-256</a></>}
        {config.repositoryPublic && <a class="button" href={`${repository}/blob/main/dev-docs/development.md`}>Build from source ↗</a>}
        <a class="button" href={releases}>GitHub Releases ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    {config.releaseAvailable && <section class="download-section" id="install">
      <h2>Install with Homebrew</h2>
      <p>Requires <a href="https://brew.sh/">Homebrew</a>. Choose one option. If you already have TeX, keep it and install only the missing tools.</p>
      <h3>FerMatter + Typst</h3>
      <p>For Typst and CeTZ; no TeX installation needed.</p>
      <InstallCommand label="Typst" command={`${app}\nbrew install typst`} />
      <h3>Full TeX Live + Typst</h3>
      <p>MacTeX without GUI apps includes the full TeX Live package set, including TikZ. Best for existing papers with many packages.</p>
      <InstallCommand label="full TeX Live" command={full} />
      <h3>Smaller TeX setup + Typst</h3>
      <p>BasicTeX plus the packages FerMatter uses. The command explicitly includes TikZ (<code>pgf</code>); add packages or fonts if your paper needs more.</p>
      <InstallCommand label="BasicTeX" command={minimal} />
      <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">TeX option</th><th scope="col">Installer download</th><th scope="col">Installed TeX files</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Full MacTeX</th><td>≈6.4 GB</td><td>≈10 GB</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">BasicTeX + packages above</th><td>≈134 MB + extra packages</td><td>≈0.5–1.3 GB</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
      <p>October 2026 estimates: BasicTeX’s base installer is about 98% smaller. Installed size varies with documentation and packages. Typst, conversion tools and Homebrew’s download cache are additional.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.tug.org/mactex/currentpackages-tug.html">Installer sizes ↗</a> · <a href="https://mirror.ctan.org/systems/texlive/tlnet/tlpkg/texlive.tlpdb.xz">TeX Live package-size metadata ↗</a> · <a href="https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf">TikZ/PGF ↗</a></p>
      <p>MacTeX and BasicTeX conflict in Homebrew; install one. Installation may request your administrator password. Restart FerMatter after installing the tools.</p>
    </section>}
    <section class="download-section" id="requirements"><h2>Before you start</h2><ul><li>Apple Silicon Mac; macOS 14 or later. Verified on macOS 26.</li><li>Typst CLI for Typst projects; TeX Live or MacTeX plus conversion tools for LaTeX.</li><li>Compiler paths can be selected in first-launch setup or Settings.</li><li>Windows and Linux builds are not available yet.</li></ul><a href={guide('requirements')}>Full requirements and tool installation →</a></section>
    <section class="download-section" id="samples"><h2>Sample projects</h2><p>Open a sample ZIP directly in FerMatter.</p><div class="sample-list">{samples.map(sample => <a href={href(`downloads/demo-${sample.id}.zip`)} download><span>{sample.name}<br/><small>{sample.detail}</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>)}</div></section>
    <section class="download-section" id="statistics">
      <h2>Downloads</h2>
      {stats ? <><div class="stats-total">{total.toLocaleString('en-US')}</div><p>Installer downloads recorded by GitHub Releases.</p><p class="stats-date">Last updated <time datetime={stats.updatedAt}>{new Date(stats.updatedAt).toISOString().slice(0,10)} UTC</time></p>{totals.size > 0 && <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Release</th><th scope="col">Downloads</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[...totals].reverse().map(([version,count]) => <tr><th scope="row">{version}</th><td>{count.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>}<p><a href={href('stats/downloads.json')}>Download the data (JSON)</a></p></> : <p>No public installer statistics yet.</p>}
      <details><summary>What is counted?</summary><p>GitHub's download counters for published installer assets, including previews. Repeat downloads count again. Source archives, sample projects, checksums and drafts are excluded. Counts are not the number of users or installations.</p><p>Snapshots refresh daily. Previously observed counts are retained if an asset is removed; downloads before our first observation of a deleted asset cannot be recovered. If collection fails, the last successful snapshot and its date stay visible.</p><p>No visitor analytics, tracking cookies, or browser calls to GitHub are used.</p></details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Product>
